{# <twig:c975LCard:Back back="{{ back }}" [still] [plain] [format="square"] [controller="site-back"] [class="..."]>the site's own content</twig:c975LCard:Back> - a card's back: the picture (an <img> the CSS stretches over it, the CSP refusing style=""), a thin rule, the frame, leant by the pointer. "back" holds "image", "tone", "effect" and optionally "label" (what a screen reader says); its tone and effect become classes for the site to draw (see BackStyleProviderInterface), "controller" naming the site's own Stimulus controller when it draws on a canvas (see assets/js/back-canvas.js). "format": "card" (63/88, or "--back-ratio") or "square". "plain" keeps the shape alone, the site laying all it wants on it: no picture, rule, frame, lean nor controller. "still" draws it for paper, without any controller #}
{% props back, still = false, plain = false, format = 'card', controller = null %}
{% set effect = back.effect ?? 'none' %}
{% set tone = back.tone ?? 'none' %}
{# @symfony-lsp-ignore stimulus.unknown_controller (registered by CardBundle's controllers.js, which lsp:check does not read) #}
<div {{ attributes.defaults({class: 'card-back card-back--' ~ effect ~ ' card-back--tone-' ~ tone ~ ('square' == format ? ' card-back--square') ~ (plain ? ' card-back--plain'), 'aria-label': back.label ?? null}) }}{% if not still and not plain %} data-controller="card-back{{ controller ? ' ' ~ controller }}"{% endif %}>
	{% if not plain %}
		<div class="card-back__picture">{% if back.image ?? null %}<img src="{{ back.image }}" alt="" loading="lazy">{% endif %}</div>
		<span class="card-back__rule"></span>
	{% endif %}
	{% block content %}{% endblock %}
</div>
